1
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:09,509
[JIMMY bothered]

2
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:12,179
Criminy. What the hell do I do?

3
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,097
You'd better not be lying.

4
00:00:14,473 --> 00:00:15,682
[growling]

5
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:16,767
[phone vibrating]

6
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:20,020
[MOMO] When you growl,

7
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:22,147
you look like
a purebred Human-Faced Dog.

8
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:23,357
Huh?

9
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,108
[MOMO] Poor Jimmy.

10
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:27,653
Fushigi's harsh words
must have hurt your feelings.

11
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,655
How'd you know?

12
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:31,448
[MOMO] I'm a very special
version of Momo.

13
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:34,326
That a fact?

14
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,495
[MOMO] Perhaps you would like
me to tell you exactly

15
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,289
what your hooded partner
truly thinks about you.

16
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:41,541
I sure ain't gonna stop you.

17
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,543
[MOMO] Soon, but not right meow.

18
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:44,544
[groans]

19
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:46,088
You're on my nerves!

20
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,506
Better not let him see you!

21
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:49,675
Ha!

22
00:00:57,641 --> 00:01:01,144
[♪ upbeat music playing,
Shikao Suga "Kageboushi"]

23
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:28,023
Hello there.

24
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,441
Hello!

25
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:30,734
Betcha thought I'd chicken out.

26
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:34,321
I can't believe
how pretty the view is here.

27
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,739
[MIKU] Now I'm jealous.

28
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,115
What are we waiting for?

29
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:38,533
It's time.

30
00:02:38,617 --> 00:02:40,243
Come in so we can
summon Bloody Mari.

31
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:41,745
[MIKU] Ready when you are!

32
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,212
[MIKU] Thanks for the invite.

33
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:51,671
I tried it by myself yesterday,

34
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:53,882
but then I got scared
and couldn't finish.

35
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,551
It was really nice of you
to agree to do this with me.

36
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:58,387
[RIMA] The living room
is back here.

37
00:02:58,845 --> 00:02:59,805
[MIKU] Great!

38
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:01,556
[MIKU noticing]

39
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:04,434
There's only a mirror?

40
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,103
Of course, silly.

41
00:03:06,395 --> 00:03:07,896
[RIMA chuckles]

42
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,815
All we need to go through
with this is a mirror

43
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:11,441
so I just removed
everything else.

44
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:12,567
[MIKU] Oh.

45
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:13,985
[RIMA] Don't sweat the details.

46
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:15,237
Excited?

47
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,738
We're about
to summon Bloody Mari.

48
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,115
[MIKU] Cool.

49
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:20,367
[eerie music]

50
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,620
[MIKU] Wait, why is it cracked?

51
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:25,038
[RIMA chuckles]

52
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:26,790
I accidentally knocked it over.

53
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:30,419
I doubt a few tiny little cracks
will stop it from working.

54
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,546
It's fine, we can work
with what we have.

55
00:03:32,838 --> 00:03:33,797
[MIKU] But is that-

56
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,173
[RIMA gasps] Don't look!

57
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:36,633
Are you okay, Rima?

58
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,594
Sorry, I guess
I got carried away.

59
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:41,388
You were starting to scare me.

60
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,598
You've always had a thing
for urban legends,

61
00:03:43,682 --> 00:03:46,560
and that's why you've been eager
to summon Bloody Mari, right?

62
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:47,686
[MIKU hesitant]

63
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:50,272
[BLUE UMBRELLA MAN laughing]

64
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:52,774
This particular book
is quite fascinating.

65
00:03:52,858 --> 00:03:54,734
I especially recommend
reading the part

66
00:03:54,818 --> 00:03:56,570
about the legend of Bloody Mari.

67
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,280
[unsettling laugh]

68
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,031
You've waited forever,

69
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:02,492
so how about we hurry up
and summon her?

70
00:04:02,576 --> 00:04:04,494
[nervous] Yeah, you're right.

71
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:06,037
We've waited long enough.

72
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:08,206
[unsettling giggle]

73
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,417
[RIMA] First, you have to look
at your own face

74
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,420
in the mirror
for 13 whole seconds.

75
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,338
[MIKU] Um, right, sure.

76
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:17,591
[RIMA] Miku, something wrong?

77
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:19,509
I don't know.

78
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:21,428
I guess
it's just a little scary.

79
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:24,097
But I've always been fascinated
by urban legends.

80
00:04:24,181 --> 00:04:25,640
Don't wimp out on me.

81
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:27,726
I didn't have to put
my neck on the line

82
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:29,436
and stick up for you like I did.

83
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,729
[worried]

84
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,314
[RIMA] Come on,
nobody else in class

85
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,316
believes in
all that urban legend stuff

86
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:35,650
you love so much.

87
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:37,068
Isn't that true?

88
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:39,321
That really bothers you,
doesn't it?

89
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:42,532
But now we're friends
and we have each other.

90
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:44,075
[MIKU sighs]

91
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,661
[MIKU] I'm sorry,
I shouldn't be scared.

92
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:49,122
I'm ready. Let's do it!

93
00:04:50,499 --> 00:04:52,918
Okay, stare at your reflection
for 13 seconds.

94
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:53,627
Right.

95
00:04:54,336 --> 00:04:57,672
One, two, three, four,

96
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:01,510
Five, six, seven,

97
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:04,554
eight, nine, ten,

98
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,598
eleven, twelve,

99
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:08,266
thirteen.

100
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:09,184
Thirteen.

101
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,646
[MIKU breathes deeply]

102
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,064
Now the next part.

103
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:16,566
Say "Come out Bloody Mari"
thirteen times, yeah?

104
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:18,068
I know.

105
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:19,236
Don't stall.

106
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,197
[MIKU inhales]

107
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,199
[BOTH] Come out Bloody Mari.

108
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,660
[BOTH] Come out Bloody Mari.

109
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,496
Come out Bloody Mari.

110
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,581
Come out Bloody Mari.

111
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:34,292
Come out Bloody Mari.

112
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:35,460
[eerie music]

113
00:05:35,544 --> 00:05:37,963
Come out Bloody Mari.

114
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,173
Come out Bloody Mari.

115
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,260
Come out Bloody Mari.

116
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,137
Come out Bloody Mari.

117
00:05:46,221 --> 00:05:48,557
Come out Bloody Mari.

118
00:05:49,391 --> 00:05:51,184
Come out Bloody Mari.

119
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:53,770
Come out Bloody Mari.

120
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:56,189
Come out-

121
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,233
Why'd you stop?

122
00:05:58,316 --> 00:05:59,609
You need to say it once more.

123
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:00,986
Yeah, I know.

124
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,153
I just need a minute.

125
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:03,238
[RIMA] Don't ruin it.

126
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:05,240
Keep going! One more time!

127
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,992
I gotta go! To the restroom!

128
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,076
[door opens]

129
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,160
[scoffs]

130
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:13,081
I hope she's not mad at me.

131
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:15,417
I really do appreciate
her becoming

132
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,127
my new urban legend buddy.

133
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:18,587
[noticing]

134
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,171
Bet that's her room.

135
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:23,341
Huh?

136
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:24,509
[MIKU] What the heck?

137
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,012
[shaking]

138
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,269
Why is it empty?

139
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:35,520
[RIMA] What are you doing?

140
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:36,730
[MIKU startled] Rima!

141
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:39,441
[RIMA] I asked you a question.

142
00:06:40,692 --> 00:06:41,401
I don't know.

143
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:42,611
[RIMA] You coward!

144
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,614
Stop messing around
and summon Bloody Mari!

145
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:47,115
[RIMA surprised]

146
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,700
[MIKU resisting] Let me go!

147
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:50,410
Talk to me!

148
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:52,203
[MIKU] You're acting
really weird.

149
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:55,957
[unsettling laugh]

150
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:57,667
[RIMA] I trust
you know the legend.

151
00:06:57,751 --> 00:06:59,669
[MIKU] Mm.

152
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:02,088
About a little girl who lived
in a town just like this one.

153
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,215
[RIMA] Both of her parents
had jobs

154
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:05,675
that kept them very busy.

155
00:07:05,759 --> 00:07:08,303
So, they always came home
late at night.

156
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,680
One day,
the girl's parents said,

157
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:13,183
"We promise that we'll be home
early today."

158
00:07:13,725 --> 00:07:15,101
It was her birthday,

159
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:17,562
and the promise of the one gift
she wanted most

160
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:18,980
filled her with joy.

161
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,316
Before her parents returned,

162
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,318
she decided
to get all dressed up

163
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:24,361
for the occasion.

164
00:07:24,903 --> 00:07:27,030
There was a lone mirror
in the living room.

165
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,407
As she gazed at her reflection,

166
00:07:29,491 --> 00:07:32,285
she noticed a dark figure
looming behind her.

167
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:34,496
"Who could it be?" she thought.

168
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:36,206
"I'm the only one home."

169
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,499
She turned around

170
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:39,167
and discovered
something horrifying.

171
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,418
[dramatic sting]

172
00:07:40,502 --> 00:07:42,712
A large man
was standing before her.

173
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:45,048
He was there to rob the house.

174
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:48,134
Before she could react,
he lunged right at her.

175
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:49,678
He cut her with his knife.

176
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:52,472
Stab! Stab! Stab!

177
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:56,101
The helpless girl
was stabbed again and again.

178
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,269
Finally,
soaked in her own blood,

179
00:07:58,353 --> 00:07:59,479
she collapsed.

180
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:02,315
"Mom and Dad promised
they'd be home soon."

181
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:06,194
"Any minute, they'll burst in
and call an ambulance."

182
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,239
She tried to endure
the excruciating pain

183
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:11,616
as she waited
for her parents to return.

184
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,575
[clock ticking]

185
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:13,702
Time passed.

186
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:16,246
But the little girl's parents
never arrived.

187
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,666
She couldn't tear her eyes
away from the mirror,

188
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:21,960
gazing at her own
blood-soaked body

189
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,712
as her consciousness
slipped away.

190
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:27,048
"Not fair, not fair, not fair!"

191
00:08:27,132 --> 00:08:28,466
Those were her last thoughts-

192
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,468
As she died alone.

193
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,470
And the girl,

194
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:34,973
she became Bloody Mari?

195
00:08:37,726 --> 00:08:39,102
[MIKU yelps]

196
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:43,189
Why did you do that?

197
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,357
[startled]

198
00:08:45,275 --> 00:08:47,026
This is all your fault!

199
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:48,319
W-What? What did I do?

200
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:50,530
You only called out
to me 12 times

201
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,116
and then refused
to finish what you started!

202
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,409
[MIKU whimpering]

203
00:08:54,743 --> 00:08:57,078
[panicking]

204
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,372
[frantic horror music]

205
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:02,500
[MIKU] Please, no! Rima?

206
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,461
[MARI scoffs]

207
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:05,712
[MIKU] Are you
really Bloody Mari?

208
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:09,299
You only called me
12 times before you stopped.

209
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:10,633
Your cowardice pulled me

210
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,303
into this world
in a broken body!

211
00:09:14,179 --> 00:09:17,056
[MIKU petrified]

212
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:19,726
I masqueraded
as a friend to fix my face,

213
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:23,063
but I should've known better
than to count on you!

214
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:26,065
I order you to finish
what you started!

215
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:27,358
Say it one more time!

216
00:09:27,442 --> 00:09:29,569
[screaming]

217
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:32,614
[breathes heavily]

218
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:36,743
[panting]

219
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:40,622
[eerie music]

220
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:46,127
Is she gone?

221
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:50,048
[MARI in demonic voice]
Call out to me one more time!

222
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,258
[MIKU shocked]
Stop! Where are you?

223
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:55,053
[MARI] Call out to me right now!

224
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:58,473
The thirteen time!

225
00:09:58,556 --> 00:10:01,309
[MIKU screaming]

226
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,019
No!

227
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:06,189
[MIKU whimpering]

228
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,274
[screaming]

229
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:10,693
-[MARI] Say it one more time.
-[MIKU] Please let me go!

230
00:10:14,739 --> 00:10:15,949
[FUSHIGI] Come with me.

231
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:17,116
[MIKU sighs]

232
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,410
Wait, how are you?

233
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:21,120
Does that really matter
right now?

234
00:10:21,204 --> 00:10:22,580
Come with me
if you want to live.

235
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:24,082
I, um--

236
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:27,544
[MARI] Call out to me!
Just one more time!

237
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,129
My name!

238
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:32,465
She has to say my name!

239
00:10:32,549 --> 00:10:36,302
[chanting a spell]

240
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:39,430
[surprised]

241
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:43,184
[MARI laughs sinisterly]

242
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,563
Fushigi!

243
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:49,607
[MARI] Call my name thirteen--

244
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:53,111
[grunts]

245
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:59,576
Holy guacamole!
That was too damn close!

246
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:02,287
Jimmy, what have you gone
and done now?

247
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:04,664
I was just trying
to save my buddy's tail is all.

248
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:05,665
Save me?

249
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,042
Because of you, she escaped.

250
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:09,752
[speechless]

251
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,588
She may have given up
on this one girl,

252
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:13,673
but now she's going to go
somewhere else

253
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:16,509
and find some other poor soul
to say her name 13 times.

254
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,094
You really think so? [huffs]

255
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,638
All you do is disappoint me.

256
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,265
Fushigi.

257
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:29,647
[crows cawing]

258
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:30,982
[JIMMY sighs]

259
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:33,735
I'm sure
in a pretty pickle now, huh?

260
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:35,194
[sighs]

261
00:11:35,904 --> 00:11:37,113
[phone vibrating]

262
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:42,327
[MOMO] You must be kitten me
with all those sighs.

263
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,495
You deserve happiness.

264
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:47,123
[JIMMY] Your idea of happiness
is pure torture.

265
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,542
[MOMO] Would you happen
to be unsettled

266
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:51,169
by the thought of splitting up

267
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:52,837
because Fushigi
is upset with you?

268
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,839
Don't take it personally.

269
00:11:54,923 --> 00:11:57,216
Searching separately
is simply more efficient.

270
00:11:57,759 --> 00:11:59,010
[JIMMY sighs]

271
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,303
You don't understand.

272
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,596
[JIMMY] It ain't like that.

273
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:03,723
We didn't split up
in the name of efficiency.

274
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,352
See, I guess I'm having
a hard time looking at him

275
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:08,978
and talking to him, maybe.

276
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:12,273
But you don't know
how it feels to care, do you?

277
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:16,569
[MOMO] I can help you
if that's what you desire.

278
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,404
No way!

279
00:12:18,488 --> 00:12:20,365
Old Jimmy wasn't born
yesterday, you know.

280
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:24,035
I ain't buying a damn thing
you're selling!

281
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:25,578
[MOMO yelling]

282
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:26,621
Oh, by the way--

283
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:28,414
What now?

284
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:30,541
[MOMO] There's a very suspicious
girl standing nearby.

285
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:35,546
I wanna go see
the cherry blossoms

286
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,340
by the river with Natsukawa.

287
00:12:37,966 --> 00:12:39,759
I bet he'll say yes
if I ask him.

288
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:42,804
We'll go and see them,
become good friends,

289
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:45,098
and then maybe
we'll even start dating.

290
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:45,682
[giggles]

291
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:46,683
[JIMMY] Hey!

292
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:48,726
Down here!

293
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,645
-[SAKURA] A dog?
-I ain't a dog.

294
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,730
I'm Jimmy
the Human-Faced Dog, okay?

295
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:54,565
Huh? That's crazy.

296
00:12:54,649 --> 00:12:56,442
Things like that don't exist.

297
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:58,152
Really?
That's rich coming from--

298
00:12:58,236 --> 00:12:59,320
[NATSUKAWA] Nailed it.

299
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:01,155
[SAKURA] It's Natsukawa!

300
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:03,282
[excited] Wait!

301
00:13:03,366 --> 00:13:04,575
Ain't ever easy.

302
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,995
[SAKURA] Natsukawa!

303
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:08,663
[panting]

304
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:10,289
Hey, what a surprise to see you!

305
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:12,208
Oh yeah, my name is Sakura,
by the way.

306
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,419
And I was wondering
if you'd maybe want

307
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,129
to go look
at the cherry blossoms

308
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,380
by the river with me?

309
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,382
[eerie music]

310
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:23,469
[SAKURA] Wait, come back!

311
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:25,471
Answer me! Please!

312
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:31,310
Natsukawa! Don't go!

313
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:32,395
[SAKURA screaming]

314
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,024
[SAKURA confused]

315
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,568
You don't even know
what you are.

316
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,653
What are you talking about?

317
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:42,405
[JIMMY] Look close.
Then you'll see.

318
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,782
[SAKURA] My hands,
what happened?

319
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:47,118
Nobody around here
can see you, kid.

320
00:13:47,201 --> 00:13:49,037
Hate to say it,
but they can't feel you

321
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,329
or hear you neither.

322
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:51,539
What do you mean?

323
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,416
You can obviously see me!

324
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:55,460
That's true,

325
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:57,628
but it's only because we happen
to be two cursed peas in a pod.

326
00:13:57,712 --> 00:14:00,381
Wait, are you telling me
I'm actually dead?

327
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,258
Was there some kind of accident?

328
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,551
Or did I get sick?

329
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:05,303
[groaning in pain]

330
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,140
Uh, are you gonna be all right?

331
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,516
[SAKURA] Don't get in my way!

332
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:12,727
Is it too much to ask,

333
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,979
to go see the cherry blossoms
with him?

334
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,231
[JIMMY] Hey! Come back!

335
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:19,525
[SAKURA] I'm a ghost.

336
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:20,693
But how?

337
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:22,236
I don't get it.

338
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,321
I can't remember.

339
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,657
Though, I remember
wanting to see

340
00:14:26,741 --> 00:14:29,577
the cherry blossoms
with him so badly.

341
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:31,329
[SAKURA noticing]

342
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:32,288
It's him!

343
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,001
It doesn't matter
if I'm a ghost now.

344
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,711
I want to be with him-

345
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:40,797
and see
the cherry blossoms together.

346
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,217
Hmm.

347
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:47,261
That girl, is she around here?

348
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:49,388
[MOMO] Indeed.

349
00:14:49,472 --> 00:14:52,100
She most likely went to the home
of the boy named Natsukawa.

350
00:14:53,768 --> 00:14:56,395
If I don't reel her in quick,
things are gonna get messy here.

351
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:58,564
[MOMO] Your destination
is on the left.

352
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,525
Your destination is on the left.

353
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:04,654
The window on the second floor
is the boys' room.

354
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:06,614
[JIMMY] Way up there?

355
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:10,034
[MOMO] The girl is currently
inside of said room.

356
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:11,285
Already?

357
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:13,538
[MOMO] I know
how you can get there.

358
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,039
-[phone vibrating]
-Huh?

359
00:15:15,123 --> 00:15:16,624
You can easily reach
the second floor

360
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:18,918
by climbing the tree
in their yard.

361
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:19,710
[JIMMY shocked]

362
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:22,255
I can climb trees?

363
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,465
[MOMO] You can do anything
you put your mind to!

364
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:26,050
[determined]

365
00:15:26,134 --> 00:15:27,343
Darn tootin'!

366
00:15:28,094 --> 00:15:29,095
[JIMMY] It's huge!

367
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:30,513
Do not count yourself out.

368
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:33,349
Use your special
Human-Faced Dog powers.

369
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:43,276
Are you sure
this is one of my powers?

370
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,277
[MOMO] Paw-sitive.

371
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,570
You're almost there.

372
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:48,114
[panicking]

373
00:15:53,703 --> 00:15:54,579
Oh boy.

374
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:55,371
Oh, whoa!

375
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:57,248
Ahh!

376
00:15:58,457 --> 00:15:59,667
That hurt like the dickens!

377
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,002
[MOMO] What a klutz.

378
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,086
[JIMMY] Shut the hell up!

379
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,629
You told me to climb!

380
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:05,506
[JIMMY] I was missing key data.

381
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:07,091
Meaning?

382
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:09,343
[MOMO] It seems
dogs are far inferior to cats.

383
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:11,387
[scoffs] What does
the internet know?

384
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:14,223
[JIMMY] Don't underestimate
a former newshawk!

385
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:15,391
I won't give up!

386
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:17,977
This juicy scoop belongs to me!

387
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:20,396
Perfect! I should post it.

388
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:24,108
[NATSUKAWA laughs]

389
00:16:24,192 --> 00:16:25,443
Will you come with me,

390
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:27,361
to see the cherry blossoms,
Natsukawa?

391
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:28,404
Hmm?

392
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:30,656
[NATSUKAWA]
Thought I heard someone.

393
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,533
Wait, did he just respond to me?

394
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:35,786
Please listen!

395
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:37,455
I should start
by telling you my name.

396
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,581
It's Sakura.

397
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,209
[SAKURA sighs]
Guessing he can't hear me.

398
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,336
No fair!

399
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,588
I just wanted to see
the cherry blossoms with him!

400
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:46,756
[startled]

401
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:50,218
What is that voice in my head?

402
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,427
Is someone there?

403
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,472
That means you can only hear me

404
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,557
when I talk about seeing
the cherry blossoms?

405
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:58,559
[breathes heavily]

406
00:16:58,643 --> 00:17:00,645
Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

407
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:02,563
[NATSUKAWA screaming]

408
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,440
No! That voice-

409
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:05,483
What is it?

410
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,526
Why is it haunting me?

411
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:09,362
So you can hear me!

412
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:12,448
[SAKURA] Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

413
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:16,661
[screaming]

414
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,455
Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

415
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:21,082
[screaming]

416
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:23,334
Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

417
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,961
[screaming]

418
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:26,754
Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

419
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,508
[SAKURA] Let's go and see
the cherry blossoms together!

420
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:34,512
Don't you want to see
the cherry blossoms?

421
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:39,267
Tell me you want to go
to see the Cherry blossoms.

422
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:40,643
I-

423
00:17:41,102 --> 00:17:42,061
[gasps]

424
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:45,231
Want to go see
the cherry blossoms.

425
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:46,315
[gasps happily]

426
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:47,566
Hooray!

427
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:50,653
[giggles excitedly]

428
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:52,113
[SAKURA noticing]

429
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,407
Wait for me!

430
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,326
[JIMMY grunts]

431
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:00,955
All right, just a little bit
further and I'm there.

432
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:02,540
Come on!

433
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:04,583
I learned to climb for nothing!

434
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:05,918
Damn it!

435
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:07,461
Hold up! Don't go nowhere!

436
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:10,506
[groaning]

437
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:12,466
[MOMO] Hey, Jimmy.

438
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:14,385
That looks like a very fun game.

439
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,345
I would like to play, too!

440
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:19,473
I ain't playing a game!

441
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:20,725
We gotta stop them!

442
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:27,148
Hurry, we're almost there!

443
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:28,608
Hurry, we're almost there!

444
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,484
You can stop walking.

445
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:32,570
We're here!

446
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:37,116
At last, I'm seeing
the cherry blossoms with you.

447
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:41,537
Finally, I'm seeing
the cherry blossoms with you.

448
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:44,332
[SAKURA] I'm seeing
the cherry blossoms with you.

449
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,583
[JIMMY] Stop right there!

450
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:46,667
Huh?

451
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:48,961
[SAKURA] You're that weird dog.

452
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:50,629
Keep your mitts off that boy!

453
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,423
I just--

454
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,342
[JIMMY] Yeah, I heard.
But you're gonna ruin his life!

455
00:18:54,425 --> 00:18:57,053
No! I would never.

456
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,055
That's bull!

457
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:01,223
[JIMMY] You were about to put
a deadly curse on the poor kid!

458
00:19:02,016 --> 00:19:03,517
A curse? On him?

459
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,937
[screams in agony]

460
00:19:08,189 --> 00:19:09,065
No way!

461
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,067
I'm supposed to be a ghost,

462
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,236
but why are these
the only memories I have of him?

463
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,030
None of it makes any sense!

464
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,531
[JIMMY] Listen up.

465
00:19:17,615 --> 00:19:19,200
You're only confused
because you're convinced

466
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:20,493
you're the ghost of a human.

467
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:21,827
[SAKURA] Huh?

468
00:19:21,911 --> 00:19:24,121
Truth is-
you ain't a ghost at all.

469
00:19:24,205 --> 00:19:25,748
You're part of this cherry tree!

470
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:28,084
[SAKURA] I'm part of the tree?

471
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,378
[JIMMY] This thing feeds
on human blood.

472
00:19:30,461 --> 00:19:32,671
And it's been guzzling
for hundreds of years.

473
00:19:33,214 --> 00:19:35,383
It's a Cursed Ubazakura!

474
00:19:35,466 --> 00:19:37,301
[SAKURA] This tree is cursed?

475
00:19:37,677 --> 00:19:39,053
It's always been a mystery

476
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:41,180
how it got its victims
to pay a visit.

477
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:43,224
Guess it's by projecting
a form like you.

478
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,142
So that means.

479
00:19:45,226 --> 00:19:46,644
[laughing]

480
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:49,397
I'm just a lonely cherry tree?

481
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:53,192
Am I not allowed
to fall in love with him?

482
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,860
[crying]

483
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:57,196
If he stays here with you,
the curse will kill him.

484
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,407
But the feeling
of loving Natsukawa-

485
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,325
means the world to me.

486
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,911
And it's made me very happy!

487
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:04,829
[startled]

488
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:05,621
[JIMMY] Take it easy!

489
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:08,040
[SAKURA screaming]

490
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:09,458
[JIMMY screaming]

491
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:13,129
[laughs] I'm sorry.

492
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:15,339
Please forgive me.

493
00:20:15,423 --> 00:20:17,425
Back off! Don't do it!

494
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:22,012
Poor Natsukawa,
I really am sorry.

495
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:25,141
[laughing maniacally]

496
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:27,476
You said you were in love
with the kid!

497
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,353
If that's true, you gotta stop!

498
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:30,521
[SAKURA] I am.

499
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,565
I love this boy to death.

500
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:33,607
[struggling] Think!

501
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:36,402
[JIMMY] Does this look
like love to you?

502
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,697
[SAKURA laughing maniacally]

503
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,369
My Natsukawa!

504
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:47,705
I love you!

505
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,206
[laughing]

506
00:20:52,877 --> 00:20:56,297
Let the kid go!

507
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:59,800
[growling]

508
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:01,761
[barking]

509
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,513
[FUSHIGI] You've done enough.

510
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:06,557
Huh?

511
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,437
[screaming]

512
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,521
It's over.

513
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:17,651
[chanting a spell]

514
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:19,153
Break!

515
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:33,501
[SAKURA screaming]

516
00:21:43,219 --> 00:21:44,178
[JIMMY sighs]

517
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:46,263
[FUSHIGI sighs]

518
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:47,473
You okay?

519
00:21:48,182 --> 00:21:49,141
[relieved]

520
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,267
[laughs]

521
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:53,729
Never better.

522
00:21:55,898 --> 00:21:58,234
Let's go to the next town.

523
00:21:59,235 --> 00:22:00,194
[JIMMY groans in pain]

524
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:02,321
[JIMMY pondering]

525
00:22:06,659 --> 00:22:09,078
[BLUE UMBRELLA MAN]
It's only a matter of time.

526
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,079
Huh?

527
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:12,581
What's that supposed
to mean, huh?

528
00:22:12,665 --> 00:22:14,375
[unsettling laugh]

529
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:15,918
It won't be very long

530
00:22:16,001 --> 00:22:18,087
until your human soul
completely slips away

531
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:20,714
and leaves nothing behind
but a Human-Faced mongrel!

532
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:22,216
Are you serious?

533
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:23,676
Once you've shed your humanity

534
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,387
and become
a pure Human-Faced Dog,

535
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,347
not only will you
forget your friends,

536
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:30,057
you'll attack them!

537
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:33,477
Just like that poor
cherry blossom girl did.

538
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:35,354
[unsettling laugh]

539
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:36,480
[JIMMY shocked]

540
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:40,568
Very soon, you too will join
the ranks of the urban legends

541
00:22:40,651 --> 00:22:42,736
as a full-fledged creature
of the night,

542
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,280
forever and ever!

543
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:45,447
[unsettling laugh]

544
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:46,448
No!

545
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:53,414
[unsettling laugh]

546
00:22:55,249 --> 00:22:56,584
Wait, come back.

547
00:22:57,418 --> 00:22:58,460
[FUSHIGI] Something wrong?

548
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:01,171
I swear I just saw-

549
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:02,256
[frustrated]

550
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:07,553
[JIMMY surprised]

551
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:11,348
You're in too much pain to walk.

552
00:23:11,432 --> 00:23:12,474
That ain't it.

553
00:23:19,315 --> 00:23:20,608
It won't happen.

554
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:22,526
Ever!

555
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,195
[JIMMY] I won't become
a monster.

556
00:23:25,279 --> 00:23:26,530
No matter what!

